<title>UK: Lehman Brothers set warrants on four German stocks.</title>
<headline>Lehman Brothers set warrants on four German stocks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers Finance has issued 20 million European-style call warrants, in four equal tranches, on BASF AG, Deutsche Bank AG, Commerzbank AG and Deutsche Telekom AG, lead manager Lehman Brothers Bankhaus AG said.</p>
<p> WARRANTS		STRIKE	  ISS PRICE</p>
<p> BASF		    60.0	    8.70 DEM</p>
<p> COMMERZBANK	   45.0	    7.00 DEM</p>
<p> DEUTSCHE BANK	 80.0	    7.95 DEM</p>
<p> DEUTSCHE TELEKOM    32.0	    7.50 DEM</p>
<p> MATURITY DATE   30.DEC.97		 PAYDATE	30.JAN.97</p>
<p> LISTING	   FFT STG DDF	     MIN EXER LOT 100</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
